- Eval: 4 positive queries (Q1, Q2, Q3, Q3f), 1 meta, 1 negative.
- Results:
  bm25 R@10 0.125, R@50 0.688, Hit@10 0.500, MRR 0.260, nDCG@10 0.123
  dense R@10 0.312, R@50 0.750, Hit@10 0.500, MRR 0.202, nDCG@10 0.169
  hybrid R@10 0.250, R@50 0.688, Hit@10 0.500, MRR 0.308, nDCG@10 0.188
- Detail:
  Q1 paracétamol dosage: dense R@10 1.0 MRR 0.25 nDCG 0.431; bm25 R@10 0 MRR 0.038; hybrid R@10 0 MRR 0.077.
  Q2 ibu+aspirine: bm25 0/0/0; dense R@50 0.5 MRR 0.025; hybrid R@50 0 MRR 0.014.
  Q3 long mission: bm25 R@10 0.25 R@50 0.75 MRR 0.5 nDCG 0.246; dense R@10 0 R@50 0.5 MRR 0.034; hybrid R@10 0.75 R@50 0.75 MRR 0.143 nDCG 0.360.
  Q3f focused: bm25 0.25/1.0/0.5/0.246; dense 0.25/1.0/0.5/0.246; hybrid 0.25/1.0/1.0/0.390.
- Source composition: Q3/Q3f top-10 all thesaurus (good). Q1 dense 9/10 nomenclature. Q2 thesaurus 7/10.
- Negative Q5: top-3 random thesaurus chunks (topotecane, laxatifs, anticholinesterasiques) → system must abstain; needs a relevance threshold/out-of-scope detector.
- Meta Q4: random thesaurus chunks.

Analysis points:
1. Dense best recall@10 (0.312) — semantic matching helps on paraphrased/long queries (Q1 dosage, Q3f).
2. BM25 strong when exact rare tokens present (Q3 class terms), near-zero on synonym gap (Q2: aspirine vs acide acétylsalicylique; ibuprofène vs AINS).
3. Hybrid RRF best MRR (0.308) and nDCG@10 (0.188), and best on the real mission question Q3 (R@10 0.75) — complements both.
4. Failure modes:
   - Synonym/abbreviation gap (Q2).
   - Verbose multi-step query dilutes dense (Q3 dense R@10 0) while BM25 handles rare terms.
   - Long aggregated chunks penalize BM25 length normalization (Q1 rank 26).
   - Out-of-scope queries return random but confident-looking chunks → need abstention (Week 4).
   - No direct amlodipine+AINS entry; evidence is class-level (AINS+antihypertensives) → needs graph reasoning (Week 3) to link amlodipine→antihypertensive class.
5. Attempted stemming (PyStemmer) regressed BM25 (associer→associ collision) → reverted; documented.

Next steps:
- Week 3: entity normalization/synonym dictionary (aspirine→acide acétylsalicylique, ibuprofène→AINS, brands→DCI), knowledge graph linking substances to classes, query decomposition.
- Week 4: LLM + retrieval + citations, relevance threshold/abstention, conflict handling (Q4), out-of-scope refusal (Q5).
- Optional: reranker (cross-encoder), better embedding model (BGE-M3), BM25 b tuning.

