- BM25: best MRR (0.179); excels when exact rare tokens (Q3 class names) but fails on synonyms (Q2 = 0).
- Hybrid: best on real mission Q3 (R@10 0.75, nDCG 0.36) and focused variant (MRR 1.0), but on tiny set its aggregate MRR is dragged down by Q1/Q2; shows complementarity.
- Failure modes: Q2 synonym gap (aspirine vs ACIDE ACÉTYLSALICYLIQUE; ibuprofène vs AINS); Q3 verbose dilution for dense; Q1 BM25 length normalization on long aggregated chunk; Q5 out-of-scope returns random chunks → need abstention; Q4 conflict needs meta-reasoning; no direct amlodipine+AINS entry → class-level evidence requires graph link.
